📘 1. Objective
This document outlines the requirements for collecting, monitoring, and alerting on critical metrics for the SAP BusinessObjects (BOXI) application deployed on AWS EC2 instances. The intent is to establish a comprehensive monitoring framework that provides visibility into the health, performance, and usage of both the underlying infrastructure and the BOXI application itself. This ensures timely detection of issues, improved application reliability, and proactive system maintenance.
🧩 2. Scope
This document covers:

EC2 host-level metrics (infrastructure)

BOXI application-level metrics

Report/job execution metrics

Security and user access activity

Log monitoring requirements

Dashboarding and alerting expectations

🖥️ 3. EC2 Host-Level Metrics (via CloudWatch Agent)

Metric Name	Source	Collection Method	Frequency	Alert Threshold
CPUUtilization	CloudWatch Agent	EC2/CloudWatch	1 min	> 85% for 5 mins
Memory Utilization	CloudWatch Agent	Custom Metric	1 min	> 80% for 5 mins
Disk Usage (%)	CloudWatch Agent	Custom Metric	5 mins	> 90%
Disk Read/Write Ops	CloudWatch	Default	5 mins	High trend
Network In/Out	CloudWatch	Default	5 mins	Unusual spikes
📦 4. BOXI Application Metrics (via CMC, Logs, or Scripts)

Metric Name	Component	Collection Method	Frequency	Alert Threshold
Job Queue Length	Adaptive Job Server	Script/API	5 mins	> 50 jobs
Report Execution Time	Web Intelligence Server	Log parsing/Audit DB	15 mins	> 5 mins/job
Failed Scheduled Jobs	Adaptive Job Server	Script/Log Analysis	10 mins	> 3 failures/run
Memory Usage per Service	All BO Services	OS Monitoring	5 mins	> 85%
Number of Concurrent Users	CMS/Audit DB	SQL Query	10 mins	> 50 users
DB Connection Failures	Connection Server	Log/Trace Monitoring	5 mins	Any
License Usage	CMS Logs/Audit DB	Log Parsing	Daily	Near limits
📄 5. Report-Level Monitoring (via Audit DB or Schedules)

Metric Name	Collection Method	Frequency	Alert Threshold
Report Success/Failure	Audit DB Query	15 mins	> 5 failed/hour
Report Run Time	Audit DB / Log Parsing	15 mins	> 5 mins (avg)
Report Schedule Delays	Audit DB / BO Schedules	30 mins	> 10 mins delay
🔐 6. Security & Access Monitoring

Metric Name	Collection Source	Frequency	Alert Threshold
Login Failures	Audit DB / Auth Logs	10 mins	> 3 failures/user
Inactive Accounts	Audit DB / CMS Query	Weekly	Inactive > 60 days
Concurrent Logins	CMS Logs / Audit DB	15 mins	> 2 sessions/user
🪵 7. Log Monitoring (BOXI Logs)

Log File Name	Path	Monitoring Goal
aps_<node>.log	<BO Install Dir>/logs/aps/	Service errors
event.log	<BO Install Dir>/logs/	Warnings/Errors
reporting.log	<BO Install Dir>/logs/	Job/report failures
trace.log	<BO Install Dir>/logs/	Debug/Deep troubleshooting
stdout.log	AppServer Logs	Tomcat/Server issues
Use CloudWatch Logs Agent, Filebeat, or log forwarders to ship logs to monitoring platforms (e.g., ELK, CloudWatch Logs, Splunk).

📊 8. Dashboards & Alerting Requirements
Dashboards should include:

System health overview (CPU, Memory, Disk, Network)

Application health (Job queues, failed jobs, login trends)

Report KPIs (avg report run time, success/failure rates)

User activity and security audit

Alerts should be configured for:

High CPU/memory

Job/report failures

Login anomalies

Disk near full

Send alerts to: [Slack, Email, PagerDuty, etc.]

✅ 9. Acceptance Criteria
Metrics are collected and visible on the dashboard

Alerts are triggered as per thresholds

Logs are searchable and retained for X days

Documentation is available for metrics and alert sources

